---
layout: default
---
<!--
  Local override of al_folio_core's _layouts/cv.liquid.

  The gem template calls {% raw %}{% al_folio_cv_render %}{% endraw %}, which renders a full CV from
  assets/json/resume.json (contact table, experience, education, ...). This
  page instead shows only the contact/profile icons - the same set the about
  page renders via jekyll-socials - so the CV itself is the linked PDF. The
  header download-PDF icon is intentionally omitted because the CV icon below
  already links to the same file.
-->

<div class="post">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
    {% if page.description %}
      <p class="post-description">{{ page.description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <article>
    <div class="social cv-social">
      <div class="contact-icons">{% social_links %}</div>
      {% if site.contact_note %}
        <div class="contact-note">{{ site.contact_note }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% comment %}
      Visitor map. This lives in the layout rather than in _pages/cv.md because
      the CV page's body content is never rendered. The snippet is the one the
      MapMyVisitors dashboard provides, with the tracker id taken from
      _config.yml; blanking visitor_map.tracker_id hides the whole box.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% if site.visitor_map.tracker_id %}
      <div class="infobox visitorbox">
        <p class="infobox-lead">
          Thanks for stopping by. The map shows how many people have visited this site and where they are reading from, courtesy of
          <a href="https://mapmyvisitors.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MapMyVisitors</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="visitor-widget">
          {% if site.visitor_map.widget == 'image' %}
            <a href="https://mapmyvisitors.com/web/{{ site.visitor_map.web_id }}" title="Visit tracker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <img
                src="https://mapmyvisitors.com/map.png?cl=080808&w=500&t=tt&d={{ site.visitor_map.tracker_id }}&co=ffffff&ct=808080"
                alt="Map of visitors to this site"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            </a>
          {% else %}
            <script
              type="text/javascript"
              id="mapmyvisitors"
              src="https://mapmyvisitors.com/map.js?cl=080808&w=500&t=tt&d={{ site.visitor_map.tracker_id }}&co=ffffff&ct=808080&cmo=3acc3a&cmn=ff5353"
            ></script>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  /* The CV page is intentionally sparse, so give the icons more presence
     than on the about page. */
  .cv-social {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cv-social .contact-icons {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .cv-social .contact-icons a {
    margin: 0 0.4rem;
  }

  .cv-social .contact-note {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Visitor map box, styled to match the info boxes on the other pages. */
  .visitorbox {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--global-divider-color, #e8e8e8);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background-color: var(--global-card-bg-color, #fafafa);
  }

  .visitorbox .infobox-lead {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--global-text-color, #1c1c1c);
  }

  .visitor-widget {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .visitor-widget img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
